{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"756","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Travel Card"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A new innovative ticketing systems for public transport is introduced in Bytesburg. Now there is a single travel card for all transport. To make a trip a passenger scan his card and then he is charged according to the fare."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The fare is constructed in the following manner. There are three types of tickets: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" a ticket for one trip costs "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"20"},{"kind":"text","text":" byteland rubles, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" a ticket for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"90"},{"kind":"text","text":" minutes costs "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"50"},{"kind":"text","text":" byteland rubles, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" a ticket for one day ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1440"},{"kind":"text","text":" minutes) costs "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"120"},{"kind":"text","text":" byteland rubles. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that a ticket for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" minutes activated at time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be used for trips started in time range from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t + x - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", inclusive. Assume that all trips take exactly one minute."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To simplify the choice for the passenger, the system automatically chooses the optimal tickets. After each trip starts, the system analyses all the previous trips and the current trip and chooses a set of tickets for these trips with a minimum total cost. Let the minimum total cost of tickets to cover all trips from the first to the current is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the total sum charged before is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then the system charges the passenger the sum "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a - b"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to write a program that, for given trips made by a passenger, calculates the sum the passenger is charged after each trip."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains integer number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of trips made by passenger."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains the time of trip "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ ti ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":"), measured in minutes from the time of starting the system. All "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" are different, given in ascending order, i. e. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ti + 1 > ti"},{"kind":"text","text":" holds for all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ i < n"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers. For each trip, print the sum the passenger is charged after it."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n10\n20\n30\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"20\n20\n10\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\n13\n45\n46\n60\n103\n115\n126\n150\n256\n516\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"20\n20\n10\n0\n20\n0\n0\n20\n20\n10\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, the system works as follows: for the first and second trips it is cheaper to pay for two one-trip tickets, so each time "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"20"},{"kind":"text","text":" rubles is charged, after the third trip the system understands that it would be cheaper to buy a ticket for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"90"},{"kind":"text","text":" minutes. This ticket costs "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"50"},{"kind":"text","text":" rubles, and the passenger had already paid "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"40"},{"kind":"text","text":" rubles, so it is necessary to charge "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":" rubles only."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"756B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/756/problem/B"}